From 4b21412ba2dd28c5cbabea07d8f9004e6dfd9a3e Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: SergiioB <119968745+SergiioB@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Wed, 18 Nov 2026 23:39:56 +0100
Subject: [PATCH] xpu(qwen27): W4A8 prompt GEMMs for groups of 64 (MLX 4-bit)

XPU_PREFILL_INT8=1 now also covers the MLX g64 checkpoint. The int8 kernel
folds its int32 partial sums once per weight group, so the group is a
generator option (64 or 128): words, A reads, scales and the bias pass follow
it. The activation quantizer scales and sums per group of q.GS (64: two groups
per 128-value block, reduced within each half of the subgroup). The runner
gates on w.gs == q.GS instead of 128; W4A4 stays at 128. The g128 zebins are
byte-identical to before. The option stays off by default.

One Arc Pro B70, dev runner, 7,976-token prompt: 4.59 s off, 3.75 s on.
With the option on, drafted == serial, the verify test and the seam test
pass. Int8 activations can change greedy text against fp16 activations.
